# NO BLANKET *.md / *.cls RULE. #334: the blanket pair used to live here, and it silently
# swallowed CLAUDE.md when that was added (#310) — `git add -A` skipped it without a word, and
# only the commit diff not matching the commit message revealed it. Tracked docs survived only
# because ignore rules do not apply to already-tracked paths, so every NEW doc needed an
# exception or a -f. That is a failure answered as a negative fact (see CLAUDE.md), in the one
# place where the failure is a file quietly not existing for anyone else.
#
# Scratch files are ignored BY NAME or BY DIRECTORY below, never by extension. If you need a new
# scratch pattern, add the narrowest one that covers it — a rule that can swallow a document is
# not worth the typing it saves. `documentation_shaped_paths_are_not_ignored` enforces this.
/Bench/
/EvalDemo/
/EvalDemo.*
/ListFilter.cls
/MyApp/
/example_patient*
/fixed_query*
/src/
/tests/Test/
.iris-dev/

# The scratch names above are ROOT-ANCHORED with a leading slash. #334: unanchored, git matches such
# a pattern at EVERY depth, so `MyApp/` also hid crates/iris-agentic-dev-core/tests/fixtures/MyApp/ —
# a directory with two tracked fixtures, where a NEW fixture was silently skipped by `git add -A`.
# `src/` did the same to the Rust crate sources, which is why this file used to carry
# `!crates/*/src/` exceptions; anchoring removes the cause, so those exceptions are gone with it.
# Add a scratch rule as `/name/`, not `name/`, unless you genuinely mean it at any depth.
